00:00:05.019 --> 00:00:06.849 align:start position:0%
European ministers responsible for  telecommunications will debate this week  ways to limit mobile telephone roaming  charges and barriers to service  providers doing business across the EU  the debate is part of efforts to improve  regulation of the telecommunications  sector and is aimed at helping to  increase competitiveness in Europe as  the digital economy grows the sector  could also develop into a major employer  particularly of young people The  ministers will examine other proposals  from the European Commission to improve  consumer protection standardized  products for operators to smooth their  entry onto the market and limits on  telephone call charges the proposals if  adopted by the council and the European  Parliament would help to complete the  digital single market by 2015 ministers  will also assess the progress made on  improving air passenger rights the  Commission has proposed ways to clear up  gray areas on rules concerning the  rights of people whose flights are  delayed or cancelled and to boost  complaint handling regulations but the  goal is also to limit the burden on  airlines in part by dealing with the  high costs that some of these  obligations might impose on carriers in  exceptional circumstances  you
 

